  "skill_summaries": {
    "ultimate": "charge up, slash in range for damage plus a portion of damage taken during charge, gaining life drain",
    "skill1": "drain HP from highest HP enemy, increasing own HP",
    "skill2": "revive once at partial HP after defeat",
    "skill3": "energy recovery from attacks; higher before revive triggers",
    "skill4": "absorb a portion of damage for bonded ally; on defeat, bonded ally sacrifices HP to revive self",
    "skill5": "ultimate additionally drains HP from enemy"
  },
  "play_overview": "[[Thoran]] charges a slash that adds part of the damage taken during the charge, then gains Life Drain on release. He drains HP from the highest-HP enemy to swell his own pool and revives once at partial HP after his first defeat. Attack-based Energy recovery is higher before the revive, fueling faster early ultimates. He absorbs part of the damage for a bonded ally, and that ally can sacrifice HP to revive him after defeat. This durable frontliner underperforms when enemies deny drain targets or burst through the first life before the revive matters.",
  "counter_overview": "[[Thoran]] plunders the highest-HP enemy, banks a revive, and is Unaffected while charging his ultimate; do not bank on interrupting that channel. A pact ally behind him can also spend HP to bring [[Thoran]] back once. Cut Vitality or healing received with [[filter:heal-inhibitor]] like [[Frieren]] or [[Gwyneth]] through both recovery windows, then delete the pact partner with [[filter:backline-assassin]] like [[Ravion]] or inhibit it with [[filter:backline-inhibit]] like [[Bonnie]]. Burst this frontliner with high-damage melee like [[Himmel]] or [[Zandrok]] before revive pays off, and avoid feeding Soul Plunder with your highest-HP unit."
}
